WEBVTT

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:19.870
Enough. There's no way I'll win.
I know that much.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:25.910
So I'll just delete your victory--and my defeat.

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:48.660
Attaboy, King of Destruction!

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:53.870
--C'mon, Masters! You can do it!
--Please... save us!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.620
Magic Range Extension.
Magic Power Magnification.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.580
Magic Designated Area
Magnification. Magic Conceal.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.910
And some MP for each of
the magic magnification skills.

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:11.120
Let's see... I'll go with 50,000 apiece.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:14.330
Mud Clap.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:37.290
A little too much.
Could have used a third of that.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.620
You okay, buddy?

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.040
Been hangin' your head for a while there.

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:47.250
Oh, that. An insect down there caught my eye.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:53.700
Too much of all this has been
entirely unexpected.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:55.910
I mean...

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:58.660
...is that King of Destruction
even playing fair?

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.080
Take <i>that</i>!

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:16.790
All those shells he's firing off
must have cost him 3 billion lir.

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:23.290
My monsters didn't come cheap, either--
at least we both felt <i>that </i>pinch.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:31.040
Why isn't he firing at Pandemonium?

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.580
If he'd wanted to, I'm sure he could
have shot down my Embryo

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:37.700
before it spat out all 50,000 monsters.

00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:45.200
It makes no sense. Is there
something else he's after?

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:55.080
You've just <i>got </i>to be out in front
of it all, don't you, Ray?

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.750
I have some unfinished business, that's all.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:09.160
"Chapter 13: Those Who Bind the Possibilities"

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:18.580
Wow, Ray's brother has one amazing Embryo.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.290
Is that...?

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:30.000
Better than standing around fretting, anyway.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.410
Ray Starling has reached
the top portion of Pandemonium.

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:37.910
He has, eh?

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:43.410
There something I have to ask Franklin...
and something I need to do.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:48.290
Will you lend me a hand
so I can get to where he is?

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:52.040
Do whatever you think you have to do.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.950
I'll get this under control,
no matter how things shake out.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:58.750
That's a big brother's job.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.000
Let me ask you a question, Ray Starling.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:07.580
Do you know the Master named Shu Starling?

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.830
He's my big brother.

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:15.450
The older sibling's a Superior,
the younger one a Maiden-wielder.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:18.750
An all-too-familiar tale.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:25.080
So why'd you come all this way?
With your brother's help, no less.

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.080
For three reasons.

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:28.910
Dear me! That many?

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:32.120
I bet I know one of them, though.

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:34.540
You came to rescue <i>her</i>, right?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:40.120
After all, your big brother can't destroy
Pandemonium with her here.

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.000
And? Your second reason?

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.040
I have something to ask you.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.700
A question? For me?

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:51.660
Who are the tians to you?

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.500
Oh, this again?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:05:00.000
That whole thing about <i>Infinite</i>
<i>Dendrogram </i>being a world or a game?

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.370
Right, right!

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.910
Anyone who thinks this is
just a game is either an idiot

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:20.000
or a child who believes everything they're told.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:25.290
How <i>could </i>it be a game? Reality. Modeling. Life!

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:30.330
Apart from the system aspects, every facet
goes well beyond the level of any <i>game</i>.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:35.660
Frankly, if it weren't for the system
constantly <i>telling </i>us it's a game,

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:37.870
you'd never recognize it as such.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:40.540
Even I don't know know exactly what it is.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:46.540
I reckon it's a plan to build a virtual world
on a national--no, a global scale,

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:51.040
and we're in the human-experimentation phase.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:56.580
Not very likely, considering how far that is
beyond our current cutting-edge tech.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:02.200
Maybe it's another world that really
does exist, like some people say--

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:06.830
or maybe... maybe aliens are involved somehow!

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:10.830
And the people who <i>live</i>
in this world? What are they?

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:15.200
AI with sophisticated minds that make
them indistinguishable from humans.

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:19.950
Or real live people from another world.
Or equivalent lifeforms.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:24.200
More than a collection of
alternating bits, at least.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.200
So let me make this clear:

00:06:26.200 --> 00:06:33.870
Even if this were Earth, with my same
situation, conditions, and abilities?

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:38.160
I would <i>still </i>have done the exact same thing.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.870
Even if it meant the death of thousands.

00:06:40.870 --> 00:06:46.370
Is <i>that </i>what you wanted to ask me, Ray?

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:52.910
A Maiden's Master like you must've wondered
why I'd plot something so vile.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:58.790
How could you <i>do </i>such a thing?!

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:06.000
Because I'm done losing.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.330
I'm done being the one who's manipulated.

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:15.540
I've decided to crush anyone
who interferes in the way I live my life.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:17.200
Is that so?

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.250
So! That takes care of your second reason.

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.250
What's your third?

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:23.830
It's--

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:31.330
Guess he must have run out of patience.

00:07:31.330 --> 00:07:34.540
I still have the princess, though, so-- Eh?

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.950
It couldn't have been Ray--
I've been watching him this whole time.

00:07:40.950 --> 00:07:43.330
The Superior Killer.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:45.080
I get it now.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.790
You were a decoy, too.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.500
Talk about intense!

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.830
They've already taken care of it.

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:10.540
The King of Destruction showed up to
kill me instead of the two I'd expected,

00:08:10.540 --> 00:08:13.540
so I had a feeling this would happen.

00:08:13.540 --> 00:08:20.000
Xunyu's ultimate skill from that battle
would make it no trouble at all.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:24.580
If only there were a way for
me to escape--and me alone...

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:28.580
Too late for that.

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:31.250
All that cannonfire has left its mark.

00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:34.500
They <i>are </i>brothers, after all.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:38.790
They might have planned this
in advance, but even if they didn't,

00:08:38.790 --> 00:08:42.290
each knew what the other would do.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:44.750
Now I'm jealous.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:49.040
I guess his third reason was to defeat me.

00:08:49.040 --> 00:08:52.200
Ah, well. I suppose I lose, then.

00:08:52.200 --> 00:08:54.000
But one day...

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:04.660
Huh?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.870
Hugo!

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:15.660
Ray, build up your damage counter
or you'll never get through that armor.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:20.000
I'm about to be reckless, Nemesis.
Are you with me?

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:21.910
Ray...

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:24.620
I sure am. Leave this to me, Master!

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:28.080
I'll protect my sister!

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.290
This is where I defeat you!

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:36.410
Bring it on, Hugo!

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:39.330
Motor Slash!

00:09:41.790 --> 00:09:44.660
Not done yet!

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.410
Motor Slash!

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:56.250
Here--have an arm!

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:57.870
"Ray Starling"

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:08.080
Vengeance Is Mine!

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:24.160
Now for my third reason...

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:26.410
I'll take care of that right now!

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:30.870
Franklin!

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:44.540
We'll win next time.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:11:01.660
You really are one reckless Master...

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:29.080
I'm sorry. My recovery magic
can't restore a missing limb.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.160
I'm just glad you managed to put
my right arm back together.

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:37.040
As far as I know, the only one in
the kingdom who can heal that wound

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:41.200
would be the High Priestess, Tsukuyo Fuso.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.830
But I really wouldn't recommend her!

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:59.040
Well, my right arm's okay--and now I know
I can hold my sword with my mouth, too.

00:11:59.040 --> 00:12:01.370
This is just fine for now.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:06.540
Does that count as a kiss?

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:12.910
And so Franklin's game came to an end,
with the kingdom as the victor.

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:17.620
--Cheers!
--Cheers, grizz!

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:27.950
Grrrizz! This exhaustion is nothing
a drink or two can't fix!

00:12:27.950 --> 00:12:32.580
Nice work tonight.
Drinks are on me, so don't be shy.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:33.910
You too, Xunyu.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:38.580
Thanks. I'm underage, though,
so I'll stick to soft drinks.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:41.950
So who in the arena wound up
making a move in the end?

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:46.370
I smashed the core of the one below
before it even got started.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:51.200
Nothing from the King of Beasts,
the Physically Strongest.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:55.790
But Caldina's Magically Strongest,
The Earth, apparently did do something.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.250
"Apparently"?

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:01.950
The monster I'd destroyed
wasn't moving a muscle.

00:13:01.950 --> 00:13:06.290
Once it was over, I used a skill to
check below the dirt in that area...

00:13:06.290 --> 00:13:08.250
...and found this.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:15.540
Dirt with a Binding spell that he
must have Multi-Activated.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:19.870
There's no way you could move
with <i>that </i>stuff hardened around you.

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:23.120
Why did those two even come, I wonder?

00:13:23.120 --> 00:13:30.410
Well, I'm guessing that the King of Beasts
had a goal entirely separate from Franklin's,

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:36.160
while The Earth came because he knew
about Franklin's terror attack.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.500
Not the other way around?

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:40.660
Well, it could be.

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:45.120
But the King of Beasts is considered
the mightiest in the three western nations.

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:48.870
If she were collaborating with Franklin on this,

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:54.540
the terrorism plan itself would have been
designed around the King of Beasts.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:13:55.870
True.

00:13:55.870 --> 00:14:01.750
Conversely, since The Earth--Fatoum was
interfering in a portion of Franklin's plot,

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:05.540
it makes sense that that's why
he came in the first place.

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:10.660
Still, the Physically Strongest
and the Magically Strongest?

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:15.410
I haven't taken on either of them directly--
are they really <i>that </i>great?

00:14:15.410 --> 00:14:18.790
You've fought The Earth before, right, Shu?

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:23.540
Oh, I've heard rumors! Who won, hmm?

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:26.040
It was... a draw?

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:28.000
Why the head-tilt?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:31.540
Our fight had the side effect of
destroying a created dungeon.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.870
Humpty and the environmental
control AI had to call it off, grizz.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:39.250
What the heck?

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:44.080
If he came all this way,
he could've at least said hi.

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:52.620
This is delicious!

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.870
I'll have to get the boss to make one someday.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:02.250
This trip to the kingdom
took longer than I'd expected.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:05.250
My original goal took no time at all,

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:10.330
but then the King of Toys suggested I arrange
the blockade around the royal capital.

00:15:10.330 --> 00:15:12.540
Then I heard about the Empire's terror plot

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:16.500
and wound up visiting Gideon
to put a stop to <i>that</i>.

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:20.750
Oh, I never did meet up with Shu, did I?

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:24.200
Well, what can you do?

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:27.370
I would only have wanted to fight him.

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:33.200
I'm having you leave the clan.

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.120
I'm... fired?

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:39.830
Seems Veldorbell will be leaving the clan, too.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:46.950
As it is, he was only in this clan
to find an honest-to-goodness hero.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:53.870
But getting swept up in my plans
means he overlooked a lot of things.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:57.200
This is all to be expected.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:00.080
I have zero popularity.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:05.790
Even before the war, AR-I-CA--the Ace--left me.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.750
Went on to become a Superior
in Caldina, I believe.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:14.500
People are... They're ditching me, all right.

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:19.750
Why'd you come help me in the end, Yu?

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:22.700
I must have milked the last drop
of your affection for me.

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:24.250
That's not--

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:28.120
You must have felt like I betrayed you.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:29.700
That's...

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:37.370
So, before you go: Why did you come
to help me atop Pandemonium?

00:16:37.370 --> 00:16:40.000
I-I mean, I don't...

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:43.700
I don't... even know...

00:16:45.660 --> 00:16:47.620
I don't know...

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:55.750
If you thought about it
and never found an answer,

00:16:55.750 --> 00:17:00.830
maybe you just acted without thinking.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:05.750
So next time, think good and hard
before drawing a conclusion--

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:09.120
a conclusion you can live
with till the very end.

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:16.000
Travel, Yu. Broaden your horizons.

00:17:16.000 --> 00:17:18.120
That's what I did back on Earth.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:18.910
Huh?

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.620
Happily, our experiences in <i>this </i>world...

00:17:21.620 --> 00:17:25.620
They won't be wasted, especially if
they deal with your nature.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:31.200
You have so much to gain from leaving
my side and traveling around.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:35.870
So go. Go now and experience
the world as you please.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:40.250
And if you want to come back
afterward, I'll be here for you.

00:17:41.500 --> 00:17:42.910
Sis...

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:45.040
Oh, and...

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:48.580
A parting gift and birthday present.

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:53.750
Don't you turn 15 this coming Tuesday?

00:17:53.750 --> 00:17:56.200
You remembered?

00:17:57.160 --> 00:18:03.290
Silly. How could I ever forget your birthday?

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.660
Oh, Francesca...

00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:14.500
Thank you, sis... I'll see you... again...

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:19.250
That's right, Yu. See you again sometime.

00:18:19.250 --> 00:18:20.660
Uh-huh...

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:30.540
That's a nice expression, Hugo.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:31.750
Uh-huh.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:35.660
I'm glad you and your sister had a real talk.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:36.950
Cyco, thank--

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:44.620
But regardless of what's on the inside,
you both <i>look </i>like adult men, correct?

00:18:44.620 --> 00:18:50.870
The sight of you two crying and speaking
in such a feminine manner, well...

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.290
It was a little weird.

00:18:58.290 --> 00:19:01.250
So <i>she's </i>out of the picture.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:06.500
The little sister I ought to love,
the person who should see my softer side,

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.830
the brakes on my conscience.

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:13.080
With her around, I couldn't pull off
anything <i>truly </i>heinous.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:16.160
Now, come hell or high water,

00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:19.950
I can claim victory over the
ones who'd defeated me.

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:24.910
You better prepare yourself, Ray Starling.

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:33.200
Her Highness is safe, and there
were no civilian casualties.

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:39.040
The Masters avenged the death
of every fallen Knight and guard.

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:44.120
They're far mightier than us tians. And yet...

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:48.540
And yet, Masters are not special.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:52.830
We really are the same after all, Lady Altimia.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.250
Lady Grandria!

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.790
What's the matter?

00:19:57.790 --> 00:19:59.830
Her Highness Elizabeth--

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:02.120
Her Highness? What happened?

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:05.750
She's left a note behind and slipped out again!

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:08.620
What?! Aw...

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:19.450
It might be hard to fight atop Silver
if I'm only holding you with one hand.

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:22.500
Right. But that's okay for now.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.120
What makes you say that?

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:26.160
This is a rematch, right?

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:31.250
We should take her on like we
did last time: Just us two.

00:20:34.290 --> 00:20:37.870
Well, <i>you're </i>certainly ready and raring to go.

00:20:37.870 --> 00:20:41.370
Go get 'em, Marie!

00:20:41.370 --> 00:20:46.200
May... May I ask what brings
you here, Your Highness?

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:50.290
You may. I'm here today to say thank you!

00:20:50.290 --> 00:20:56.830
I saw your brother the bear walking
by outside and followed him here.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.750
Grizz, grizz!

00:20:58.750 --> 00:21:01.370
Did you get permission first?

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:03.910
I sneaked out, of course!

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:10.200
Come <i>on</i>, Liliana! After what happened?!
Your security is <i>way </i>too lax!

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:13.870
At first I was like, "Not <i>this </i>again"--

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:18.450
but I've come to think Ellie's
just too good an escape artist.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:23.410
You've got talent!
You'd make a great cat burglar.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:32.370
All that aside... let's get started, shall we?

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:37.290
I like your spirit. But do you
really think you can win?

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:43.370
Well, let's see: Your level and stats
are still miles above mine.

00:21:43.370 --> 00:21:46.500
There's no comparing our skillsets.

00:21:46.500 --> 00:21:50.660
To top things off, I've lost half my battle
prowess along with my left arm.

00:21:50.660 --> 00:21:52.790
I have almost no chance of winning.

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:56.700
Still, I won't say my chances are <i>zero</i>.

00:21:56.700 --> 00:22:03.250
If there's a possibility I long for,
I won't give up reaching for it.

00:22:03.250 --> 00:22:07.250
That's what seizing the
possibility is all about!

00:22:07.250 --> 00:22:09.870
You really get it, don't you?

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:13.160
And that's why I'm fighting to win!

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:15.870
That's what makes you Ray the Unbreakable.

00:22:15.870 --> 00:22:17.700
The what now?

00:22:17.700 --> 00:22:23.250
Oh, you didn't know?
You've got a nickname now, Ray.

00:22:23.250 --> 00:22:25.790
Along with "the King of
Destruction's little brother"

00:22:25.790 --> 00:22:29.250
and "that guy even a Superior couldn't crack."

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:31.410
W-Wow, those are really, uh...

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:36.200
You've also got "Dark Paladin,"
"Prince on the Silver Steed,"

00:22:36.200 --> 00:22:41.330
and "the Light- and Dark-Wielding Hero
Clad in Violet and Crimson."

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:42.700
What's your preference?

00:22:42.700 --> 00:22:44.620
"Unbreakable"!

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:48.830
The "Prince" one isn't half bad, either.

00:22:50.200 --> 00:22:52.040
No, thanks.

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:54.830
Okay, got it. And with that...

00:22:54.830 --> 00:22:57.250
Here we go, Unbreakable!

00:22:57.250 --> 00:22:58.080
Nemesis!

00:22:58.080 --> 00:22:59.370
Right!

00:23:03.410 --> 00:23:07.040
You got yourself a fight, Superior Killer!

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:15.160
Begin quest!

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:19.790
"Tokyo"

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:24.580
"Tokyo"
Now to finish up that college
admissions process...

00:23:30.410 --> 00:23:31.950
Hi there!
